# What never enters the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile copies named directories, so today nothing below would reach
# the image anyway. This file exists for the day someone writes `COPY . .` -
# at that moment .env and lab/ would be baked into a layer, and a layer is
# permanent in whatever registry the image reaches.
#
# It also stops sending ~7 MB of .git and licensed brand art to the daemon on
# every build.

# Secrets, in every form they take here
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
lab/
credentials.json
secrets.yaml
*.key
*.pem

# Not needed to run the app
.git
.gitignore
.github
Brand/
calibration/
tools/
docs/
deploy/
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile

# Local Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Scan output: customer prompts and transcripts. Never in an image.
results/
scans/
*.scan.json
